.113725 .160784 .207843 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 39.7 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 12.1 TL (A Patient structure keeps each person's details together, so sorting or copying a patient moves one complete record instead of) Tj T* (coordinating several arrays. Functions can receive a Patient pointer to access or update one record without copying every field.) Tj T* (Nested Date and BloodPressure types make the meaning of each value clear and allow those types to be reused. New fields) Tj T* (can be added in one structure definition, reducing the risk of mismatched data.) Tj T* ET
