BT 1 0 0 1 0 39.7 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 12.1 TL (This works because the caller assigns the returned modified structure back to list[i]. With sizeof\(struct account\) typically 8 bytes) Tj T* (\(int plus float\), the source-level model transfers one 8-byte parameter copy into the function and one 8-byte return value back:) Tj T* (about 2 x 8 = 16 logical bytes per call, followed by assignment to the caller's element. The compiler/ABI may use registers or) Tj T* (optimize copies away. Pointer passing sends one pointer \(typically 8 bytes on a 64-bit system\) and updates the original directly.) Tj T* ET
